   <meiHead xml:lang="en">
      <fileDesc>
         <titleStmt>
            <title type="main">Variations for Piano, Op. 27</title>
            <title type="subordinate">I</title>
            <composer>
               <persName auth="GND" auth.uri="https://d-nb.info/gnd/118629786" codedval="118629786">Anton Webern</persName>
            </composer>
            <respStmt xml:id="resp.editor">
               <resp>Editor: encoding, correction against the print, metadata</resp>
               <persName>Egor Polyakov</persName>
            </respStmt>
         </titleStmt>
         <editionStmt>
            <edition n="0.1.0">Working digital edition, not yet proofread</edition>
         </editionStmt>
         <pubStmt>
            <publisher>CAMAT Corpus Editions</publisher>
            <date isodate="2026-10-11">2026-10-11</date>
            <availability>
               <useRestrict>MEI data released under <ref target="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</ref>. The licence covers this edition's encoding and metadata, not the musical work or the printed source.</useRestrict>
            </availability>
         </pubStmt>
         <sourceDesc>
            <source xml:id="src.ue1937" type="printed-edition">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Variationen</title>
                  <composer>
                     <persName auth="GND" auth.uri="https://d-nb.info/gnd/118629786" codedval="118629786">Anton Webern</persName>
                  </composer>
                  <edition>First edition (1937); the copy used was printed from the original plates in 1965 or later</edition>
                  <imprint>
                     <pubPlace>Wien</pubPlace>
                     <publisher>Universal Edition</publisher>
                     <date isodate="1937">1937</date>
                  </imprint>
                  <identifier type="plate">U.E. 10881</identifier>
                  <biblScope unit="page" from="3" to="5">pp. 3–5</biblScope>
                  <ref type="digital-facsimile" target="https://imslp.org/wiki/Special:ImagefromIndex/28271">IMSLP file 28271</ref>
                  <annot type="copy">
                     <p>The copy used is the scan in IMSLP file 28271 (PDF of printed pages 3–11, SHA-256 d604c08ab797818f414a83fa4047eb2eb3c52ba6c74a47ce966e0a9c273ab330). Its first page carries the 1965 copyright renewal, so it was printed in 1965 or later; a first-issue copy of 1937 has not been compared.</p>
                  </annot>
                  <annot type="paratext">
                     <p>p. 3, head: page number "3"; caption title "VARIATIONEN"; movement numeral "I"; above the first system, right: "Anton Webern, Op. 27".</p>
                     <p>p. 3, foot: "Copyright 1937 by Universal Edition" and "Copyright renewed 1965" (left); "Universal Edition Nr. 10881" (centre).</p>
                     <p>pp. 4–5: page numbers "4" and "5"; foot: "U.E. 10881".</p>
                  </annot>
                  <availability>
                     <useRestrict>Scan uploaded to IMSLP by JacopoTore (2017); scanner unknown. IMSLP lists the file as “Public Domain - Non-PD US”. The page images are not redistributed with this edition; the facsimile links point to local renderings of the PDF.</useRestrict>
                  </availability>
               </bibl>
            </source>
            <source xml:id="src.kern.sapp" type="digital-encoding">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Op. 27, I</title>
                  <editor>Craig Stuart Sapp</editor>
                  <edition n="2020-11-23">Revised 2020-11-23; encoded 2008-12-17</edition>
                  <imprint>
                     <publisher>KernScores</publisher>
                     <date isodate="2020-11-23">2020-11-23</date>
                  </imprint>
                  <identifier type="file">webern-op27n1.krn</identifier>
                  <identifier type="SHA-256">5d53373697aacdd4b752dbf2339d030a63b7074100005f2901e57f1d22906437</identifier>
                  <ref target="https://kern.humdrum.org/cgi-bin/ksdata?file=webern-op27n1.krn&amp;l=users/craig/classical/webern&amp;format=kern">KernScores</ref>
                  <annot>
                     <p>Base encoding for notes and rhythms, converted with Verovio; a starting point, not a witness. Its header notes: “no beams, dynamics, slurs, articulations”. Retrieved 2026-09-26 through kern.ccarh.org; not redistributed.</p>
                  </annot>
               </bibl>
            </source>
         </sourceDesc>
      </fileDesc>
      <encodingDesc>
         <appInfo>
            <application isodate="2026-09-27T13:26:44" version="6.3.0-425dd7b">
               <name>Verovio</name>
               <p>Converted the Kern encoding to MEI.</p>
            </application>
            <application isodate="2026-09-27">
               <name>Edirom Deep Optical Measure Detector</name>
               <p>Detected the bar regions on the page images (<ref target="https://measure-detector.edirom.de/">measure-detector.edirom.de</ref>); the facsimile zones come from its output.</p>
            </application>
            <application isodate="2026-10-11">
               <name>scripts/migrate_mei51.py</name>
               <p>Converted Verovio's MEI 6.0-dev output to MEI 5.1 by targeted text edits.</p>
            </application>
            <application startdate="2026-09-26" enddate="2026-10-11">
               <name>Claude Code</name>
               <p>Anthropic's AI coding assistant, used under the editor's direction for the facsimile linking, the MEI 5.1 migration, validation repairs and the draft of this header. Editorial decisions and responsibility rest with the editor.</p>
            </application>
         </appInfo>
         <editorialDecl>
            <p>This edition encodes the music as printed by Universal Edition, plate U.E. 10881 (src.ue1937), including stems, beams, clefs, the placement of marks, and page and system breaks. The Kern encoding (src.kern.sapp) supplied notes and rhythms as a starting point; it has no authority where it differs from the print.</p>
            <p>The print is not corrected. A suspected engraving error is kept and documented in an annot with type="editorial" and label "source-reading"; uncertain readings are labelled "unresolved-reading", and notes on the representation "encoding-note". Repairs that bring the encoding into agreement with the print are recorded in the repository's proofreading log.</p>
            <p>Every printed accidental is encoded as a written accidental (@accid); an alteration without a printed sign is encoded with @accid.ges. The values func="caution" and type="caution" left by the Kern conversion carry no editorial claim.</p>
            <p>Measure/@n is the printed bar number; the pickup of movement II is bar 0. Each measure points to its zone on the facsimile page; pb/@n is the printed page number. Page paratext is transcribed in sourceDesc; the pgHead repeats the printed head of the movement's first page for display only.</p>
            <p>The extent of proofreading is recorded in revisionDesc and in the repository's proofreading/progress.csv.</p>
         </editorialDecl>
         <projectDesc>
            <p>This edition was prepared by CAMAT Corpus Editions as part of a DFG-funded corpus for music-analysis technologies (grant PF 669/18-1).</p>
         </projectDesc>
      </encodingDesc>
      <workList>
         <work xml:id="work.op27">
            <identifier type="opus">Op. 27</identifier>
            <title xml:lang="de">Variationen für Klavier</title>
            <title type="translated">Variations for Piano</title>
            <composer>
               <persName auth="GND" auth.uri="https://d-nb.info/gnd/118629786" codedval="118629786">Anton Webern</persName>
            </composer>
            <creation>
               <date notbefore="1935" notafter="1936">1935–1936</date>
            </creation>
            <perfMedium>
               <perfResList>
                  <perfRes>Piano</perfRes>
               </perfResList>
            </perfMedium>
            <componentList>
               <work xml:id="work.op27.I">
                  <title>I</title>
                  <meter count="3" unit="16" />
                  <tempo>Sehr mäßig</tempo>
               </work>
            </componentList>
         </work>
      </workList>
      <revisionDesc>
         <change isodate="2026-10-11" resp="#resp.editor">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>The sb elements no longer carry @type="z", the name of the Humdrum layout group (!!LO:LB:g=z) that the Kern conversion copied into @type; the breaks follow the UE print (scripts/set_breaks.py).</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-11" resp="#resp.editor">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Edition header: MEI 5.1 CMN declarations, responsibility, edition, source and work metadata, editorial declaration and this revision history. It replaces the metadata written by Verovio's Humdrum import and the study's project note. The page head in the score (pgHead) now shows the printed head instead of the import's composer line and life dates.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-11" resp="#resp.editor">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Converted from MEI 6.0-dev to MEI 5.1 by scripts/migrate_mei51.py (commit 9572be9).</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-10-11" resp="#resp.editor">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Hand edits from the print (study, before the repository): stems, beams and beamSpans, slurs, dynamics, hairpins, “dim.” and “rit.” in bars 1–18; clefs, key signatures and page and system breaks for the whole movement. The clefs were first aligned with the help of a third-party encoding (DCMLab WebernNo1.mxl); checking each clef against UE 10881 is pending in proofreading. Details: provenance/movement-I-edits/EDITS.md in the repository.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
         <change isodate="2026-09-27" resp="#resp.editor">
            <changeDesc>
               <p>Study (CAMAT PDF-facsimile workflow): converted the Kern encoding with Verovio, gave all IDs the movement prefix and linked each bar to its zone on the UE page images. Provenance: provenance/ in the repository.</p>
            </changeDesc>
         </change>
      </revisionDesc>
   </meiHead>
